1. DEFINITIONS AND SCOPE

1.1 “CrownThrive Material” means CrownThrive-specific original or controlled material made available through this repository or its governed projections, including, as applicable: institutional documentation; policies; standards; registries; schemas; diagrams; taxonomies; ontologies; knowledge graphs; architecture; configuration; source-derived reconciliations; research summaries; operating methods; workflows; runbooks; product systems; business methods; licensing structures; platform descriptions; API/MCP/interface descriptions; SDK and integration designs; agent/automation governance; prompts; evaluation designs; datasets and compilations; media; music; books; curriculum; stories; visual works; characters; universes; imprints; brands; marks; product concepts; Cultural Imprint Engine materials; CHLOM materials; Thrive Flywheel materials; MM Suites materials; ThriveBase public-safe specifications; ThriveEvergreen materials; and other original CrownThrive content, except to the extent a specific item is expressly identified as Third-Party Material or separately licensed material.

1.2 “Protected Systems” includes CrownThrive-specific frameworks, architectures, interfaces, algorithms, methods, model/prompt/evaluation systems, control planes, orchestration designs, economic activation logic, rights/evidence systems, institutional registries, security designs, and other systems whether expressed in prose, diagrams, schemas, code, data structures, APIs, MCP tools, workflows, or machine-readable records.

1.3 “Machine Interfaces” includes APIs, MCP servers/tools/resources, SDKs, schemas, webhooks, event contracts, feeds, agents, plugins, command surfaces, integration adapters, and other machine-consumable interfaces.

1.4 “Marks” includes CrownThrive names, logos, claimed trademarks, service marks, platform identities, imprints, trade names, slogans, product names, trade dress, and other source identifiers.

1.5 “Restricted Institutional Material” includes credentials, secret values, private contracts, protected evidence, unreleased assets, confidential research, private economic schedules, security-sensitive configuration, private algorithms, restricted prompts, private identities, customer or personnel data, payment data, privileged communications, and other material classified as internal, restricted, strategic, confidential, privileged, or machine-only.

1.6 “Third-Party Material” means software, specifications, fonts, icons, templates, provider APIs, standards, libraries, media, examples, or other material controlled by a third party and identified by a file-level license, attribution, package manifest, provider terms, THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md, or other applicable rights notice.

